# SentinelMesh

SentinelMesh is a Windows-friendly cybersecurity portfolio project that runs adaptive deception services, fingerprints hostile sessions, correlates threat intelligence, and produces analyst-ready reports. The design came from your prompt, but the implementation here is shaped to be deployable as a strong MVP on Windows through native Python or Docker Desktop.

## What This Build Includes

- Async deception services for HTTP, FTP, SMTP, and SSH-style interaction
- Real-time behavioral profiling with risk scoring and threat IDs
- Threat-intelligence correlation hooks for OTX, AbuseIPDB, Shodan, and VirusTotal
- STIX 2.1-style bundle generation
- Adaptive shell response engine with trainable sequence prediction
- FastAPI dashboard with recent sessions, profiles, and events
- JSON and PDF report generation
- Docker, CI, pre-commit, Windows startup helper, and deployment docs

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["Attacker Traffic"] --> B["Adaptive Honeypot Engine"]
    B --> C["Session Store (SQLite)"]
    B --> D["Behavioral Profiler"]
    B --> E["Adaptive Deception Engine"]
    D --> F["Threat Intel Correlator"]
    F --> G["STIX Bundle + Reports"]
    C --> H["FastAPI Dashboard"]
    G --> H
```

